# 7. PREVENT DOUBLE BOOKINGS

This is a critical operational requirement.

Two employees must never successfully reserve the same bed or room inventory for overlapping dates.

The existing frontend checks are insufficient because two devices may make changes simultaneously.

Implement authoritative conflict protection using transactions or another reliable server-controlled booking operation.

Protect:

- Individual bed assignments.
- Whole-room reservations.
- Multiple-bed reservations.
- Overlapping dates.
- Booking modifications.
- Cancellations.
- Reassignments.
- Simultaneous reservation requests.

Check-in is inclusive and checkout is exclusive for occupancy calculations.

Cancelled or otherwise non-inventory-blocking bookings must be handled according to explicitly defined business rules.

Do not treat invalid dates as valid bookings.

Test simultaneous reservation attempts and ensure only one conflicting transaction succeeds.

